+/*
+ * Non-zero while a legacy (pre-staged) sysupgrade is in progress.
+ *
+ * The /sbin/sysupgrade of LEDE 17.01 and older announces an upgrade by
+ * calling `ubus call system upgrade` and afterwards kills every process
+ * by itself (kill_remaining) before switching over to a ramfs.  While
+ * that happens procd must not respawn any of the killed services: they
+ * would come back within respawn_timeout seconds, keep references to the
+ * old rootfs and consume memory, which makes the subsequent pivot_root()
+ * in run_ramfs fail with EBUSY or kills the box with an OOM.
+ *
+ * This flag was dropped together with the "upgrade" ubus method when the
+ * staged sysupgrade mechanism was introduced; bring it back so that old
+ * rootfs images keep working with this procd.
+ */
+extern int upgrade_running;
+
